markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Getting Ready for the Curriculum</h1>

<p>This professional learning module gives you a guided preview of the key concepts and instructional approaches used throughout the unit.</p>

<p>Think of this module as a head start: a chance to build familiarity with the ideas your students will encounter, and to start thinking about how you'll teach them in your classroom.</p>

<p>This module highlights important concepts and teaching strategies, but it doesn't replace reviewing individual lesson materials. Take time to review each lesson before teaching it with students.</p>

<h2>What's in this module?</h2>

<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 900px; margin: 25px auto;">

  <div style="background-color: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 10px;">
    <h3>Lesson 1 - Introduction to Foundations of AI Programming</h3>
    <div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 8px;">You are here</div>
    <p>This lesson provides an introduction to the Foundations of AI Programming unit and professional learning module. It offers a brief overview of course resources and features.</p>
    <p><i>10 minutes</i></p>
  </div>

  <div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 10px;">
    <h3>Lesson 2 - Computational Thinking</h3>
    <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #1F1976; margin-bottom: 6px;">Aligns to curriculum lessons 1-3</div>
    <p>This lesson explores key computational thinking concepts and how they connect to coding instruction. By understanding these concepts, you will build a strong foundation for teaching programming and discover strategies to help students develop problem-solving skills.</p>
    <p><i>20 minutes</i></p>
  </div>

  <div style="background-color: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 10px;">
    <h3>Lesson 3 - Coding Basics</h3>
    <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #555555; margin-bottom: 6px;">Aligns to curriculum lessons 4-7</div>
    <p>This lesson introduces foundational coding concepts using CodeAI's Neighborhood IDE, or programming platform. You will explore key programming elements such as variables, print statements, objects, and functions.</p>
    <p><i>25 minutes</i></p>
  </div>

  <div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 10px;">
    <h3>Lesson 4 - Advanced Algorithms</h3>
    <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #1F1976; margin-bottom: 6px;">Aligns to curriculum lessons 8-12</div>
    <p>In this lesson, you will explore key programming concepts that help control the flow of a program: while loops, if statements, and nested/two-way selection. Through interactive coding in CodeAI's Neighborhood IDE, you will learn how to break down problems using flowcharts and implement solutions with structured code.</p>
    <p><i>25 minutes</i></p>
  </div>

  <div style="background-color: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 10px;">
    <h3>Lesson 5 - Preparing for the Final Project</h3>
    <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #555555; margin-bottom: 6px;">Aligns to curriculum lesson 13</div>
    <p>In this lesson, you will focus on key instructional strategies for guiding students through their final project. You will explore effective collaboration methods, structured feedback approaches, and planning techniques to help students manage their time and workflow.</p>
    <p><i>10 minutes</i></p>
  </div>

</div>


**Total suggested time:** 90 minutes


---

## Engaging with This Module

As you move through the module, focus on building confidence with the concepts, noticing instructional strategies, and making connections to how students may experience the learning in your classroom.

Throughout these lessons, you'll also see how **AI-supported teaching strategies** connect to each concept along the way.
MARKDOWN
